authorization.explanation:
The peer task, developing the producer's retained work on the right inner section into a coherent, assessable record, is complete. Everything is retained in output/ (exposition.md, record.json with 36 claims, evidence/); the transport check passes.

Verification: all producer proofs were re-derived by hand (convexity of the first-correction interpolation G, CP1, CT1, CT2, CT3 structure, first comparison, diagonal reduction, obstacles). The producer's identities and certificates were reproduced with independent exact code, and 13 producer scripts re-ran byte-identically (one output differs only in timing).

First turn (peer additions): an independent exact table for n<=1000 whose SHA-256 matches the published table; rigorous interval certification of the registered section for all n<=3000 (new range 1001-3000); exact failure of (D_6) from n=868; the ordering of the two sufficient-condition families.

This resumed turn pursued the open analytic and finite questions:
- proved (x^5 y)'>0 for all x>0 (extends the producer's CT2 to rho<=3/20);
- gave an interval-arithmetic proof that L_(1/2) y>0 for all x>0, which with CT3 makes re79cb's critical-window support for conjecture 10.3 an informal theorem;
- found numerically the critical truncation threshold rho*~0.7504;
- determined exactly that 'S_rho>=0 for all states' holds for all n<=1000 iff rho<66/113 and is false for every rho>=66/113 (strict failure at the central-end state (458,227)), with the mechanism explained;
- ran rigorous whole-diagonal computations up to n=39996, confirming the predicted n^(-1/3) margins and showing the (D_7) central margin is borderline (limit 0+-0.2, undecided).

What remains (the registered section for n>=3001; all-n proofs of S_rho for rho<66/113 or of (D_8); explicit starting sizes) needs uniform asymptotics with explicit constants in the moving regimes (1<<r<<n^(2/3), upper critical, bulk, center). That is a separate research program, stated precisely in the record as the remaining obligation; it is not unfinished peer development. The root P remains unresolved.

